1. A blocked prompt (promptFeedback with no candidate) finishes as
   content_filter instead of ending with no terminal event.
2. A stream with no finish reason ends in a RUN_ERROR (code
   incomplete-stream) instead of no terminal event, and the chat stream's
   RUN_ERROR carries the latest usageMetadata the stream reported.
   Upstream PR to be opened for 1-2; remove when released.
3. The terminal event carries the candidate's finishReason as
   metadata.providerStopReason, so the service decides every finish reason from
   the SDK's union (apps/api/src/lib/chat/provider-stop-reasons.ts) instead
   of reading an unhandled one as "stop". Remove when upstream exposes the
   raw reason.

